<article class="env-lemma" id="03E4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03E4">Lemma <span data-tag="03E4">66.5.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Then $X$ is quasi-compact if and only if $|X|$ is quasi-compact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a scheme $U$ and an étale surjective morphism $U \to X$. We will use Lemma <a href="/tag/03H5" data-tag="03H5">66.4.4</a>. If $U$ is quasi-compact, then since $|U| \to |X|$ is surjective we conclude that $|X|$ is quasi-compact. If $|X|$ is quasi-compact, then since $|U| \to |X|$ is open we see that there exists a quasi-compact open $U' \subset U$ such that $|U'| \to |X|$ is surjective (and still étale). Hence we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>